NOTES
==============================================================================
1. Counts as run: 18/18 checks passed / VERDICT: PASS + 13/13 checks passed / VERDICT: PASS, and 6/6 mutations turned the right check red.
   Section 1 runs the same two gates against the INDEX, so the evidence
   is about the bytes being committed rather than about the working tree
   -- which also carries a parallel music change that is NOT in this
   commit. The working tree's logs (sections 2 and 3) and the index
   tree's came out identical on the readings that matter.
2. THE TWO FALSE GREENS, kept because they are the finding.
   * A3 (solo `guards: 1 -> 0`) stayed green because `guardCountFor`
     is `Math.max(1, preset.guards || 1)`: the 0 is silently coerced,
     so the mutation did not change the built world at all. Re-run as
     `1 -> 2` and the named check fires. A preset therefore cannot say
     "no guard"; standing down is the play-layer hook
     `begin(id, { guards: 0 })`.
   * B2 (marker ground ring `2.0 -> 2.6 px`) stayed green because the
     widest blob only reaches 11.54 px -- it never crosses the bar of
     12. The 2.6 value was rejected earlier for ANTIALIASING margin on
     a real canvas; that is a judgement, and it is not asserted. At
     3.5 px the blob is 12.44 and the check fires.
   Lesson: a mutation must be shown to have changed the world before
   it is used to judge a gate. Both times, the gate was right.
3. AND ONE THAT WAS NOT A FALSE GREEN BUT A POLLUTED ONE. The first
   version of the two gates wrote their log to a fixed path. A mutation
   run therefore made each gate overwrite its OWN canonical log with a
   FAILED transcript, and reverting the source afterwards did not revert
   the log -- `work/verify_packets.log` sat there reporting a failure
   that never happened to any real code. `--log` exists because of that;
   the mutation run now writes work/_mut_<tag>.log and cannot touch the
   canonical slot. "Remember to restore the log" is not a mechanism.
4. What these gates do NOT cover, and who does: pixels. Marker blob
   geometry is asserted here as DRAW CALLS; the centroid-vs-project()
   half lives in scripts/verify_play.mjs and needs a browser.
